Country and administrative-region names are derived from GeoNames,
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.
See https://www.geonames.org/ and LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.
Names have been normalized, grouped and filtered. Dataset URLs, revision
and download hashes are recorded in data/sources.json.
The Wikidata items listed under iso3166_2 in data/reference.json (their ISO
3166-2 codes) come from Wikidata, released under CC0-1.0 (https://www.wikidata.org/).

Reviewed historical membership observations in data/historical_memberships.json
cite Philippine government publications and Wikidata (CC0-1.0).
Generated historical membership observations in data/historical_memberships.tsv
(sources, checksums and retrieval dates in data/historical_sources.json) are
reduced to dated settlement-to-ancestor facts, linked to Wikidata items (CC0-1.0)
through the datasets' codes, from:
- Statistics Norway's KLASS municipality/county correspondence
  (https://data.ssb.no/api/klass/v1/), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  International: https://www.ssb.no/en/diverse/lisens and LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt;
- Insee's Code officiel géographique 2015, Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0
  (https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/);
- the ANPR archivio storico dei comuni, Ministero dell'Interno with Istat,
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (https://www.anagrafenazionale.interno.it/note-legali/).
Current boundaries and complete historical intervals are not imported.

