The evaluation corpus tests/gold.jsonl (not part of the runtime image) contains
coordinates, administrative codes and addresses derived from:
- Wikidata (CC0-1.0) and the Dutch BAG via PDOK (CC0-1.0);
- Base Adresse Nationale, licensed under Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0
  (https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/);
- the US Census Bureau geocoder (US Government work, public domain);
- the ONS Postcode Directory via postcodes.io, licensed under the Open
  Government Licence v3.0 (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/).
  Contains OS data © Crown copyright and database right. Contains Royal Mail
  data © Royal Mail copyright and database right. Source: Office for National Statistics.
Per-case sources and retrieval dates are recorded in the corpus; `evaluate build-gold` regenerates it
from tests/gold.seeds.jsonl.
Reference adjudications in docs/evaluation/adjudications/168.md also cite the US Census
Bureau's TIGERweb boundaries (US Government work, public domain), VGIN address
records, Bahrain's Legislation and Legal Opinion Commission and Ministry of
Municipalities Affairs and Agriculture, Glorious Vision University's contact
page, Nigeria's National Universities Commission register and ROR's CC0 locality
metadata. Those texts and boundary geometries are not bundled; the corrected Bahrain
code is sourced from CC0 Wikidata. The university case remains unresolved.

Registry-first and school-sampled evaluation corpora have per-source attribution and
reuse terms in tests/registry/*.NOTICE. These notices accompany the corpora and are
installed in container images under /usr/local/share/licenses/opengeocoding/registry/.

The global address source-consistency gold corpus in tests/global/ is derived from
OpenStreetMap under ODbL-1.0, with attribution and additional source terms in
tests/global/NOTICE. That notice accompanies the corpus in the evaluation image.

tests/snapshots/addresses.tsv contains geocoding results derived from OpenStreetMap
data via Nominatim. Data © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open
Database License (ODbL) 1.0: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
